    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^3+x-8$. Solve $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$ for $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=2$.\n\nSince $f'(x)=3x^2+1>0$, solve $f(x)=x$.",
      "worked": "$f'(x)=3x^2+1>0$ for every real $x$, so $f$ is strictly increasing. Its intersections with its inverse lie on $y=x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3+x-8&=x\\\\x^3&=8\\\\x&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
